<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Basic Scanning Rules and Useful Tips</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="101.057%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">While in 'S</span>can' <span lang="EN-GB">mode, to start and stop scanning press</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'</b></span><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>B'</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">button on the remote control. Patch is a sequence of stripes captured between two consecutive pressings of the</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'</b></span><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>B'</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">button.</span></p>
<table cellspacing="0" class="whs4">
<col>
<col>
<col>
<col>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td class="whs6">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="images/rules_and_tips.gif" width="183px" height="400px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td class="whs8">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="images/rules_and_tips_2.gif" width="183px" height="400px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td class="whs8">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="images/rules_and_tips_3.gif" width="183px" height="400px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td class="whs9">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="images/rules_and_tips_4.gif" width="183px" height="400px" border="0" class="img_whs7" alt=""></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td class="whs10">
<p class="caption" style="font-size:12pt;">1</p>
</td>
<td class="whs11">
<p class="caption" style="font-size:12pt;">2</p>
</td>
<td class="whs11">
<p class="caption" style="font-size:12pt;">3</p>
</td>
<td class="whs12">
<p class="caption" style="font-size:12pt;">4</p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<ul class="whs13">
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US">Press</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'</b></span><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>A'</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">button to enter '</span>Scan' <span lang="EN-US">mode.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US">KUBE will be in '</span>Pause' <span lang="EN-US">mode. Press</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'</b></span><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>B'</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">button to start scanning.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet" style="font-size:10.0pt;"><span lang="EN-US">As scanning is started, a patch is generated.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-US">Press</span> <span lang="EN-US" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>'</b></span><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>B'</b></span> <span lang="EN-US">button to enter '</span>Pause' <span lang="EN-US">mode. Patch is complete.</span></p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet">Press and hold '<span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>A</b></span>' button to delete last scanned patch</p>
</li>
</ul>
<table cellspacing="0" width="100%" class="whs14">
<col class="whs15">
<col class="whs16">
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="21.646%" class="whs17">
<p class="caption">Rule/Tip</p>
</td>
<td bgcolor="#EAE8D6" width="78.354%" class="whs18">
<p class="caption">Explanation</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td width="21.646%" class="whs19">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span lang="EN-GB">Rigidity</span></p>
</td>
<td width="78.354%" class="whs20">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">During scanning the object and localiser base must not move relative to each other.</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Use a strong bench.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Attach the object to the bench</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td width="21.646%" class="whs19">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span lang="EN-GB">Laser Reflection or Absorption</span></p>
</td>
<td width="78.354%" class="whs20">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">Shiny, glass, unpainted plastic or matt black objects do not scan well due to laser reflection or absorption.</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Use</span> <span class="Command"><a href="../../User_Interface/Scan_Pane_(Arm_Menu).htm#Autoset_Laser_power" target="_self">Autoset Laser</a></span> <span lang="EN-GB">command to detect the correct laser power level.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Try lower</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Ambient Thresholds</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">(In Hardware settings/Sensor tab).</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td width="21.646%" class="whs19">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span lang="EN-GB">How Should I Scan with ModelMaker?</span></p>
</td>
<td width="78.354%" class="whs20">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">Strip scanning is the most efficient</span></p>
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">Like using a paint spray can:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Creating a number of strips by scanning in passes.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">One passover for each area of the model with a small overlap.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Always move the sensor smoothly and consistently.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td width="21.646%" class="whs19">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span lang="EN-GB">Scanning Speed</span></p>
</td>
<td width="78.354%" class="whs20">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">Scanning speed is set by changing Point Spacing parameters.</span></p>
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">How SLOWLY can I scan?</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">If scanning very slowly, too much data will be recorded and the resulting point cloud will be very large. &#160;</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">How FAST can I scan?</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">If scanning too quickly, the data is less accurate and details on the object may be missed out.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">For more details see &#160;</span><span class="Path">Hardware Settings &gt; Real Time Processing</span><span class="Path" style="font-weight:normal; font-style:normal;">.</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td width="21.646%" class="whs19">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span lang="EN-GB">Scanning for Maximum Detail</span></p>
</td>
<td width="78.354%" class="whs20">
<p class="normal-table">The sampling is set to 1 in sensor settings so that every point on the laser stripe is recorded.</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td width="21.646%" class="whs19">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span lang="EN-GB">Scanning for Optimum Information</span></p>
</td>
<td width="78.354%" class="whs20">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">Collect very dense data on features and sparse data in between.</span></p>
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">Orientate the stripe across a feature line or an edge and follow along the line.</span></p>
<table cellspacing="0" class="whs4">
<col>
<col>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td class="whs21">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="Scanning_tips_files/image002.gif" width="178px" height="174px" border="0" class="img_whs22" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td valign="middle" class="whs23">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">Stripe at 90 degrees across a style line and across an edge.&#160;</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p>&#160;</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="21.646%" class="whs19">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span lang="EN-GB">Scanning Memory Limit</span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="78.354%" class="whs20">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">If you are scanning a large and/or very detailed object:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Save the data frequently.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Divide the object up into several areas and create one scan file for each area.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Set the Point Sampling to 2 or 4.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Note"><span lang="EN-GB">(For the detailed areas such as edges, set it back again to 1).</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Regularly check the status bar information about number of captured points and memory usage</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="../Images/status.gif" width="929px" height="28px" border="0" class="img_whs24" alt=""></span></p>
<ul>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Use the properties box</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p><span lang="EN-US"><img src="images/rules_and_tips_5.gif" width="421px" height="307px" border="0" class="img_whs25" alt=""></span></p>
<p>&#160;</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="21.646%" class="whs19">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span lang="EN-GB">Positioning -</span></p>
<p class="normal-table-func"><span lang="EN-GB">Angle</span></p>
<p class="normal-table-func">&#160;</p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="78.354%" class="whs20">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">In general keep the laser directed approximately 90 degrees to the surface.</span></p>
<table cellspacing="0" class="whs4">
<col>
<col>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td class="whs26">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="Scanning_tips_files/image005.jpg" width="315px" height="277px" border="0" class="img_whs27" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td valign="middle" class="whs23">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">Image of stripe normal to an object’s surface (annotated with an arrow).</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p>&#160;</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td width="21.646%" class="whs19">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span lang="EN-GB">Positioning -</span></p>
<p class="normal-table-func"><span lang="EN-GB">Stand-off</span></p>
</td>
<td width="78.354%" class="whs20">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">The sensor stand-off from the object depends on sensor type being used.</span></p>
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">The very best results are obtained when the laser is at its sharpest focus (this is set in the middle of the range).</span></p>
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">The following indicators can help you determine correct distance:</span></p>
<ul>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Stand-off bar - on the screen.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Stand-off laser - on the scanning object.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Stand-off LED - on the sensor (MM W range only).</span></p>
</li>
<li style="margin-left:-20px;" class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB">Stand-off probes - accessories (MM W range only).</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>&#160;</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="21.646%" class="whs19">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span lang="EN-GB">Positioning -</span></p>
<p class="normal-table-func"><span lang="EN-GB">Stand-off LED and Stand-off Probe</span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="78.354%" class="whs20">
<table cellspacing="0" class="whs4">
<col>
<col>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td class="whs6">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="Scanning_tips_files/image007.gif" width="109px" height="109px" border="0" class="img_whs28" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td valign="middle" class="whs23">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">Stand-off LED will stay lit while the sensor is within calibrated range.</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td class="whs10">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="Scanning_tips_files/image009.gif" width="190px" height="118px" border="0" class="img_whs29" alt=""></span></p>
</td>
<td valign="middle" class="whs23">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">Probe is a mechanical way of keeping the sensor at the right Stand-off.</span></p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
<p>&#160;</p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="21.646%" class="whs19">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span lang="EN-GB">Positioning -</span></p>
<p class="normal-table-func"><span lang="EN-GB">Stand-off Laser</span></p>
</td>
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="78.354%" class="whs20">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">Represents the distance between the sensor and the object, by using another laser.&#160;</span></p>
<table cellspacing="0" class="whs4">
<col>
<col>
<col>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td class="whs6">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="Scanning_tips_files/image011.gif" width="99px" height="94px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td class="whs8">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="Scanning_tips_files/image013.gif" width="99px" height="97px" border="0" class="img_whs31" alt=""></p>
</td>
<td class="whs9">
<p class="normal-table"><img src="Scanning_tips_files/image015.gif" width="99px" height="94px" border="0" class="img_whs30" alt=""></p>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td class="whs10">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">Too far away</span></p>
</td>
<td class="whs11">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">Capturing data</span></p>
</td>
<td class="whs12">
<p class="normal-table"><span lang="EN-GB">Too near</span></p>
<p class="normal-table">&#160;</p>
</td>
</tr>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
<tr valign="top" class="whs5">
<td colspan="1" rowspan="1" width="21.646%" class="whs19">
<p class="normal-table-func"><span lang="EN-GB">Positioning -</span></p>
